    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.04) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) headline our offensive output, serving as the core drivers for our stolen base and batting average targets. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** enjoys a massive efficiency boost from a favorable matchup against Pallante, benefiting from a +14% platoon advantage and a prime #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance; he faces Martinez, whose 4.85 xERA combined with a switch-hitting profile and top-tier park factor makes him our safest high-floor play. **Jacob Wilson** also continues to trend upward with a 68.83 score, as the combination of a generous matchup against Lowder and his elevated position in the #2 hole makes him an essential start over mid-tier bench options.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jorge Polanco** (53.68) on the bench. While his score remained competitive, he was narrowly edged out by the superior platoon and park factors surrounding **Liam Hicks** and **Heliot Ramos**. The optimizer prioritized **Liam Hicks**\u2019s matchup against Sugano\u2019s 5.02 xERA, which provides a significantly higher ceiling for extra-base hits compared to the matchup **Jorge Polanco** faces against the tougher Bibee. We are also monitoring several weather-related risks: **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all currently listed with a 33\u201336% rain risk. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough test against Detmers, his elite profile keeps him in the lineup, but we will need to pivot quickly if these games are delayed or postponed. Finally, note that **Jackson Merrill** remains a high-value play despite the pending lineup, as his projection relies on a favorable matchup against Bratt\u2019s porous 6.59 xERA, keeping him firmly ahead of **Miguel Vargas**, who sits on the bench due to a stiffer encounter with Gray.",
